{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1791321000000-reviewer-d14-source-gate.opus.stdout.log'","aggregated_output":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d14\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-06 22:44:20 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-07 05:44:20 +07\n\n# Gate review: M-next D14 (source/exit half with progress journal)\n\n**Verdict: NOT READY**\n\nThe new freeze/rehydrate seam does its job. It has its own tag and version 1 and reuses the handoff codec. It checks addresses, the header, descriptors, the snapshot against the body and the recovery state before anything is attached. It proves byte identity by re-preparing and re-encoding, with zero IO calls, and a recovered record cannot abort (`export.cljc:313-485`, `:527`). The exit order matches the ruling (`driver.cljc:1243-1270`). Acknowledgments are matched to the exact request: the report id carries `[o1 l address]` and the release id carries the lease (`driver.cljc:1148-1150`, `:1327-1331`, `:2292-2313`).\n\nFour defects block landing: two high-severity, two medium.\n\n## Blocking findings\n\n**1. (High) A non-admitted report answer wedges the exit forever while the lease keeps being renewed.**\n- `step-exit-body` turns any non-admitted report answer into a permanent `:report-refused` (`driver.cljc:1263-1265`). There is no resend, no run end and no release.\n- `step-active-held` still renews on every step before entering the exit body (`driver.cljc:1982-1989`). The holder therefore keeps the occurrence alive indefinitely, and it never closes or becomes regrantable.\n- `completion/report!` documents the authority's own `:suspended` and `:closed` answers. `:suspended` is transient, so it should lead to a resend. The terminal refusals (`:ended-lease`, `:quarantined`, `:report-conflict`, `:counter-regression`) should run the r3 1.6 run-end: one diagnostic plus cleanup release.\n- No test drives a refused or suspended report.\n\n**2. (High) Abort is not journaled, so a reopen brings back an aborted first export and offers its stale snapshot.**\n- `abort*` (`driver.cljc:2498-2556`) changes only the in-memory state. The journal still holds the `:first` mint and fence.\n- After a crash, `reopen` sends that journal through `reopen-source` (`driver.cljc:2415-2416`, `:2201-2227`). It rebuilds the fenced snapshot and `step-exporting` sends the offer.\n- But the aborted machine had already returned to local, uncustodied execution and may have performed IO after the snapshot. If the offer is admitted and granted, the stale checkpoint runs again: double execution and duplicated effects.\n- Abort needs a durable terminal record (for example `{:yin.k/journal :yin.k/aborted :yin.k/occurrence O}`), written before local execution is handed back. The fold and reopen must then treat it as closing the export.\n- No test reopens after an abort.\n\n**3. (Medium) A holder that crashes during exit preparation, before the fence, stays stalled forever and never releases or re-proposes.**\n- The first `reopen` branch (`driver.cljc:2405-2408`) stalls on any minted-but-unfenced occurrence, including a successor or result minted after a journaled grant.\n- `:stalled` refuses all progress, and reopening again gives the same answer. The origin lease is never released, and this driver never re-enters candidacy.\n- That contradicts:\n  - the ruling §1: \"a restarted holder releases and re-enters candidacy\";\n  - brief item 9;\n  - the new UCF text: \"they reconcile, release and re-enter candidacy\".\n- Releasing the origin lease and re-proposing over the origin checkpoint is not one of the ruling's forbidden moves (inventing waits, reminting, blind re-serving, or using the original machine). Only a `:first` source should stay non-runnable here; when a grant exists, this case belongs in `reopen-holder`.\n- `exit-journal-cuts-never-restore-execution-test` (`driver_test.cljc:2644-2679`) only asserts \"not running\" plus one step. It passes on this permanent stall and never checks that the release eventually happens.\n\n**4. (Medium) The abort tenure check ignores dao.lease's max cap and its bound latches.**\n- `abort*` computes the bound as `(or last-renewal-at granted-at) + duration` (`driver.cljc:2526-2531`).\n- dao.lease's `at-bound?` also enforces `:dao.lease/max` from `granted-at`, plus the sticky `:bound-reached?` and `:undersized?` latches (`dao/lease.cljc:1818-1832`).\n- UCF grants do carry `:dao.lease/max` (`ledger.cljc:78`, `authority/grant.cljc:153`). A holder past its cap but inside its renewal window can therefore abort back into execution. The ledger's `:live` check only closes that window once the judge's lapse has been folded.\n- The fix: decide tenure with `lease/holding?` and derive `:bound` from the same rule.\n\n## Non-blocking findings\n\n5. **(Low/Plausible) Restart cleanup can drop the exit cell.** In `step-exiting` (`driver.cljc:1297-1308`), a restarted exit clears `:exit` once release carriage is acknowledged and the ledger fold, read in the same step, does not yet show the report. If carriage acknowledgment can arrive before the earlier report is visible in the ledger, the closed occurrence's successor is never offered (the driver then answers `:not-holder` in proposing). Please confirm that the front guarantees ledger visibility before carriage replies, or keep the exit cell until the fold shows the lease ended.\n\n6. **(Low) The driver hard-codes the journal's cursor shape.** `journal-records` checks `:dao.stream.memory-log/identity` and `/position` keys (`driver.cljc:451-458`). That is backend knowledge inside the driver. It is consistent with journal.cljc's stated visible log, but brittle. Separately, malformed or unavailable history throws `ex-info` (with an `:assembly` hint) rather than returning a data refusal. That fails closed, which is acceptable, but the hint is misleading.\n\n7. **(Low/Needs confirmation) Version-1 published bytes may have changed.** `handoff.cljc:793` now runs the module-store fixed-point for `(:v1 @found)` too, not only for recovery. If a v1 body previously omitted transitive module stores, its published v1 bytes change. The ruling says \"Semantic handoff versions 0/1 and their bytes remain unchanged\", and the findings only mention leaving v0 unchanged. This needs a statement that `canonical-order` already covered these stores, or an architect note that this is a correction rather than a format change.\n\n8. **(Low) Small cleanups.**\n   - A freshly minted proposal intent is journaled twice before its first send (`driver.cljc:1407-1418`).\n   - `export-fence-step`'s eager `mapv` still stores the body after the recovery store has failed (`driver.cljc:866-881`). The fence stays correctly gated either way.\n\n9. **(Low) Seam test coverage.** `recovery-preserves-aliases-distinct-cells-and-authentic-closures-test` proves an authentic, receiver-owned closure held in the store. It does not test a closure captured in the blocked frame's environment registers, which is the ruling's \"closure inside waits\" case. Adding a `let1 'f (lam …)` / block / `(app (v 'f))` row would close that.\n\n## Regression check against D13/D11/D12\n\nI found no regression to the landed D13 candidate path: admitted-variant check, grant durable before lower, bound-before-apply renewal, run-end single diagnostic. Stall refusal covers `step`, `hand-off`, `abort` and `enroll`. Enrollment follows C12: every enroll call is preceded by a projection reread, and unavailable evidence waits.\n\nThe engineer's JVM 3556/235377 green result was not re-run, as instructed. Nothing was edited and no suite was run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2390,2565p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '1390,1440p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '1800,1850p' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; sed -n '467,563p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; rg -n 'report\"'!|suspended|ended-lease'\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/completion.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2390,2565p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '1390,1440p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; sed -n '1800,1850p' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; sed -n '467,563p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc; rg -n 'report\"'!|suspended|ended-lease'\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/completion.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   reconcile its uncertain append only here. Persisted clock readings\n   never restore tenure.\"\n  [config]\n  (let [units (or (:units config) lease/default-units)]\n    (check! (some? (:journal config)) \"a progress journal\" {})\n    (check-common! config units)\n    (let [folded (fold-journal (journal-records (:journal config)))\n          mint (:mint folded)\n          exit? (and (some? mint)\n                     (or (nil? (:grant folded))\n                         (> (:index mint) (get-in folded [:grant :index])))\n                     (contains? #{:yin.k/successor :yin.k/result}\n                                (:role mint))\n                     (contains? (:fences folded) (:occurrence mint)))]\n      (assoc (cond\n               (and (some? mint) (not (contains? (:fences folded) (:occurrence mint))))\n               (assoc (bare-state config units) :phase :stalled :status :yin.k/unsatisfied\n                      :detail {:yin.k/reason :incomplete-preparation\n                               :yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence mint)})\n\n               exit? (reopen-exit config units folded)\n\n               (some? (:grant folded))\n               (reopen-holder config units folded)\n\n               (some? mint)\n               (reopen-source config units folded)\n\n               :else (reopen-candidate config folded))\n             :enroll (:enroll folded)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Enrollment (r3 1.10; UCF 7.7.7's C12 identity discipline)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- enroll-attempt*\n  \"One bracketed enrollment step (r3 1.10; UCF 7.7.7 as amended by\n   C12): enrollment carries no request identity, so an uncertain answer\n   is reconciled by rereading the projection -- the driver enrolls\n   again only when the derived target identity is absent, because a\n   blind retry enrolls a second target.  The derived identity (the one\n   the authority's next transaction would mint) is journaled with the\n   intent; a committed answer journals the acknowledgment and answers\n   the target.  `:enroll!` is the composition's enrollment seam (the\n   authority's own enrollment, `(fn [] enrollment-answer)`).\"\n  [state]\n  (let [cell (or (:enroll state) {})]\n    (cond\n      (some? (:target cell))\n      (with-status state :yin.k/ok {:yin.k/enrolled (:target cell)})\n\n      (nil? (:derived cell))\n      (if-some [p (folded-projection state)]\n        (let [i (ledger/target-identity (:arbitration state) (:next-t p))]\n          (journal! state\n                    {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/intent\n                     :yin.k/action :yin.k/enroll\n                     :yin.k/derived i})\n          (with-status (assoc state :enroll {:derived i})\n            :yin.k/ok {:yin.k/enroll :intent :yin.k/derived i}))\n        (unsatisfied state :no-arbitration\n                     {:dao.stream/identity (:arbitration state)}))\n\n      :else\n      (let [answer (try\n                     (enroll! state)\n                     (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n                       {:yin.k/status :suspended :yin.k/reason :threw}))\n            acknowledge\n            (fn [state i]\n              (journal! state\n                        {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/ack\n                         :yin.k/action :yin.k/enroll\n                         :yin.k/target i})\n              (with-status (assoc state :enroll {:target i})\n                :yin.k/ok {:yin.k/enrolled i}))]\n        (cond\n          (= :committed (:yin.k/status answer))\n          (acknowledge state (:yin.k/target answer))\n\n          ;; uncertain: the derived identity's presence in a fresh fold\n          ;; is the commit; its absence licenses exactly one more\n          ;; attempt, never a blind retry\n          :else\n          (if-some [p (folded-projection state)]\n            (if (contains? (:targets p) (:derived cell))\n              (acknowledge state (:derived cell))\n              (let [i (ledger/target-identity (:arbitration state)\n                                              (:next-t p))]\n                (when (not= i (:derived cell))\n                  (journal! state\n                            {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/intent\n                             :yin.k/action :yin.k/enroll\n                             :yin.k/derived i}))\n                (with-status (assoc state :enroll {:derived i})\n                  :yin.k/unsatisfied\n                  {:yin.k/reason :enroll-uncertain\n                   :yin.k/derived i})))\n            (unsatisfied state :no-arbitration\n                         {:dao.stream/identity\n                          (:arbitration state)})))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Abort (r3 1.9; UCF 7.7.4 as amended)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- abort*\n  \"Return the exporting machine to local execution (r3 1.9; UCF 7.7.4\n   as amended): `attempts` are the journaled ones -- one per offer\n   attempt whose intent was durable before the send, `:append` the\n   outcome its append answered -- and a holder exporting a successor\n   aborts only with tenure `{:now n :bound b :live true}`, the ledger\n   reader's evidence and the bound.  After the lease has ended its old\n   local machine is never restored.\n\n   Answers the state over export/abort's answer: :ok restores the\n   machine (:running for a holder mid-run, :aborted for a first\n   export); a refusal leaves the source fenced, the state unchanged\n   but for the status.\"\n  [state]\n  (let [cell (or (:export state) (:exit state))\n        _ (check! (some? cell) \"an export or exit to abort\" {})\n        machine (or (:m cell) (:machine state))\n        folded (fold-journal (journal-records (journal-of state)))\n        attempts (offered-attempts folded (:occurrence cell))\n        tenure (when (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n                 (let [p (folded-projection state)\n                       l (:lease state)\n                       entry (get-in p [:occurrences (:occurrence state)])\n                       holder (:holder state)\n                       units (:units state)\n                       base (fn [d]\n                              (let [[unit magnitude] (first d)]\n                                (* magnitude (get units unit))))\n                       bound (when (and (map? p)\n                                        (some? holder)\n                                        (some? (:granted-at holder)))\n                               (+ (base (or (:last-renewal-at holder) (:granted-at holder)))\n                                  (base (:dao.lease/duration\n                                          (:grant holder)))))]\n                   (when (some? bound)\n                     {:now (base (clock state))\n                      :bound bound\n                      :live (and (= l (:dao.lease/lease entry))\n                                 (= (get-in state\n                                            [:evidence :yin.k/binding\n                                             :yin.k/epoch])\n                                    (:yin.k/epoch entry)))})))\n        r (export/abort machine (:record cell) attempts tenure)]\n    (if (= :ok (:status r))\n      (if (contains? (:machine r) :yin.k/custody)\n        (-> state\n            (assoc :machine (:machine r))\n            (dissoc :exit :export)\n            (assoc :phase :running)\n            (with-status :yin.k/ok\n              {:yin.k/aborted (:occurrence cell)}))\n        (-> state\n            (assoc :machine (:machine r))\n            (dissoc :exit :export)\n            (assoc :phase :aborted)\n            (with-status :yin.k/ok\n              {:yin.k/aborted (:occurrence cell)})))\n      (with-status state (:yin.k/status r)\n        (dissoc r :yin.k/status)))))\n\n\n(defn- enroll*\n  [state]\n  (let [cell (:enroll state)]\n    (if (and (:derived cell) (nil? (:target cell)))\n      (if-some [projection (folded-projection state)]\n        (if (contains? (:targets projection) (:derived cell))\n          (do\n\n\n(defn- propose\n  \"Send or resend the current proposal, minting a fresh id when the last\n   one was refused (7.7.8: a proposal id is answered at most once), and\n   answer the state after it: while it is unanswered the step answers\n   `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`.  A minted id's intent record is durable in\n   the journal before its first send, so a resent proposal keeps its\n   stable id across a reopen.\"\n  [state projection]\n  (let [refused? (= :dao.lease/rejected\n                    (get-in projection [:answered [(:me state)\n                                                   (:id (:proposal state))]]))\n        mint? (or (nil? (:proposal state)) refused?)\n        proposal (if mint?\n                   (let [pid (fresh-pid state)\n                         request (proposal-request (:occurrence state) pid)]\n                     (journal! state\n                               {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/intent\n                                :yin.k/action :yin.k/proposal\n                                :yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)\n                                :yin.k/request request})\n                     {:id pid :request request :sent false})\n                   (:proposal state))\n        sent? (true? (:sent proposal))\n        outcome (when-not (:carried proposal)\n                  (journal! state {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/intent :yin.k/action :yin.k/proposal\n                                   :yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)\n                                   :yin.k/request (:request proposal)})\n                  (let [answer (append-request! state (:request proposal))]\n                    (journal! state {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/action :yin.k/proposal\n                                     :yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)\n                                     :yin.k/request-id (get-in proposal [:request :yin.k/request-id])\n                                     :yin.k/append (:dao.stream/outcome answer)})\n                    answer))\n        proposal' (assoc proposal\n                         :sent (or sent?\n                                   (= :dao.stream/ok\n                                      (:dao.stream/outcome outcome))))]\n    (-> state\n        (update :sent-proposals\n                (fn [ids]\n                  (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome outcome))\n                    (conj ids (:id proposal)) ids)))\n        (assoc :proposal proposal'\n               :proposals (if mint?\n                            (inc (or (:proposals state) 0))\n                            (or (:proposals state) 0)))\n        (with-status :yin.k/awaiting-grant\n          {:yin.k/occurrence (:occurrence state)\n           :dao.lease/proposal (:id proposal')}))))\n(defn at-bound?\n  \"H3: true when the holder's reading has reached the bound -- the earlier\n  of the duration since the later of its last renewal and its observed\n  grant, and the cap the grant carries measured from the grant itself --\n  whether or not anything has been heard. The holder stops acting AT the\n  bound: equality fires here where the judge's `exceeds?` would not, so a\n  stopped holder's last renewal lands before the judge's window closes.\n  The bound is TERMINAL (P1): once reached it is latched\n  (`:bound-reached?`) and stays true for any later reading, however stale\n  or small -- a late renewal cannot buy back a lease the judge may already\n  have reclaimed. An undersized grant is at the bound from observation on.\n  False before any grant is observed: no grant, no bound, nothing held.\n  An invalid reading answers false meaning UNANSWERABLE, never free to\n  act: with no usable tick there is no bound to measure, and a flow that\n  guards on this predicate alone would act on a bound it could not see --\n  gate flows through `holding?`, which fails closed on the same input.\n  The bound bounds attention, not access (H5): this answers a question, it revokes nothing.\"\n  [holder reading]\n  (let [{:keys [grant granted-at units]} holder]\n    (cond\n      (:bound-reached? holder) true\n      (:undersized? holder) true\n      (nil? grant) false\n      (not (reading-ok? holder reading)) false\n      :else (let [duration-reached (at-or-past?\n                                     units\n                                     (interval units reading (activity-basis holder))\n                                     (get grant :dao.lease/duration))]\n              (if-some [cap (get grant :dao.lease/max)]\n                (or duration-reached\n                    (at-or-past? units (interval units reading granted-at) cap))\n                duration-reached)))))\n\n\n(defn observe-renewal\n  \"Record this holder's own renewal. The control flow appends the renewal\n  fact and hands the append's outcome here with `reading` -- the reading\n  drained BEFORE the append: a reading taken after it would move the\n  basis later than any evidence the judge can have for the renewal. The\n  activity basis advances to that reading only when the append answered\n  `:dao.stream/ok` (H2) -- a `full`, `closed` or\n  `:dao.stream/transport-error` append advances no bound, and the\n  schedule still says due, measured from where it was, so the control\n  flow retries -- AND only when the holder is not at its bound: the bound\n  is terminal (P1). A renewal that lands at or past the bound -- the\n  control flow stalled, and the judge may already have lapsed the lease --\n  latches `:bound-reached?` and moves nothing, and the latch is sticky:\n  no later stale or smaller reading reopens the lease. A renewal recorded\n  after `stop` records nothing: the holder's activity has stopped. A\n  reading that fails `reading-ok?` records nothing.\"\n  [holder reading outcome]\n(defn fold-journal\n  \"The driver's projection of its progress journal: what was minted and\n   fenced, which external actions were intended, attempted and\n   acknowledged, and which grant was accepted.  The records are the\n   driver's own grammar, plain data under `:yin.k/journal`:\n\n     {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/minted :yin.k/role r :yin.k/occurrence O\n      :yin.k/header h}\n     {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/fenced :yin.k/occurrence O\n      :yin.k/address A :yin.k/record RA}\n     {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/intent :yin.k/action a :yin.k/occurrence O\n      :yin.k/request req :yin.k/bytes-at A}   ; offer, proposal, resumed,\n                                              ; release, enroll (no\n                                              ; request identity)\n     {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/attempt :yin.k/action :yin.k/offer\n      :yin.k/occurrence O :yin.k/append outcome}\n     {:yin.k/journal :yin.k/ack :yin.k/action a :yin.k/occurrence O\n      :yin.k/request-id rid :yin.k/answer ans}  ; or :yin.k/grant, which\n                                                ; carries the lease\n\n   The fold answers\n\n     {:mint        the last minted occurrence's data, or nil\n      :fences      occurrence to {:address A :record RA}\n      :intents     request-id to the last intent record of that id\n      :acked       the request-ids whose acknowledgment stands\n      :answers     request-id to the authenticated answer\n      :attempts    occurrence to the offer attempts, {:append o} each\n      :offered     the occurrences whose offer intent stands\n      :grant       {:yin.k/occurrence O :dao.lease/lease l}, or nil}\"\n  [records]\n  (reduce\n    (fn [f [index record]]\n      (case (get record :yin.k/journal)\n        :yin.k/minted\n        (assoc f :mint {:role (get record :yin.k/role)\n                        :index index\n                        :occurrence (get record :yin.k/occurrence)\n                        :header (get record :yin.k/header)})\n        :yin.k/fenced\n        (assoc-in f [:fences (get record :yin.k/occurrence)]\n                  {:address (get record :yin.k/address)\n                   :record (get record :yin.k/record)})\n        :yin.k/intent\n        (let [rid (get-in record [:yin.k/request :yin.k/request-id])]\n          (-> f\n              (update :intents assoc rid record)\n              (update :ordered-intents conj record)\n              (cond-> (= :yin.k/enroll (get record :yin.k/action))\n                (assoc :enroll {:derived (:yin.k/derived record)}))\n              (cond-> (= :yin.k/offer (get record :yin.k/action))\n                (update :offered conj (get record :yin.k/occurrence))\n                (= :yin.k/offer (get record :yin.k/action))\n                (update-in [:attempts (get record :yin.k/occurrence)] (fnil conj []) {}))))\n        :yin.k/ack\n        (cond\n          (= :yin.k/enroll (get record :yin.k/action))\n          (assoc f :enroll {:target (:yin.k/target record)})\n\n          (= :yin.k/grant (get record :yin.k/action))\n          (assoc f :grant {:occurrence (get record :yin.k/occurrence)\n                           :index index\n                           :lease (get record :dao.lease/lease)})\n          :else\n          (let [rid (get record :yin.k/request-id)]\n            (-> f\n                (update :acked (fnil conj #{}) rid)\n                (update :answers assoc rid record))))\n        :yin.k/attempt\n        (if (= :yin.k/offer (:yin.k/action record))\n          (update-in f [:attempts (get record :yin.k/occurrence)]\n                     (fn [attempts]\n                       (check! (seq attempts) \"attempt with durable intent\" record)\n                       (assoc attempts (dec (count attempts))\n                              {:append (get record :yin.k/append)})))\n          (update f :action-attempts (fnil conj []) record))\n        f))\n    {:mint nil :fences {} :intents {} :ordered-intents [] :acked #{} :answers {}\n     :attempts {} :offered #{} :grant nil}\n    (map-indexed vector records)))\n\n\n(defn- offered-attempts\n  \"The journaled offer attempts of `occurrence` (r3 1.9): one per\n   attempt whose intent was durable before the send, `:append` the\n   outcome its append answered -- absent when none did.  An intent with\n   no attempt record is one send of unknown outcome.\"\n  [folded occurrence]\n  (let [sent (get-in folded [:attempts occurrence])]\n    (if (and (contains? (:offered folded) occurrence)\n             (empty? sent))\n      [{}]\n      (or sent []))))\n\n\n(defn- intent-of\n  \"The last intent record of `action` for `occurrence`, or nil.\"\n8:   `report!` admits the report: the reporting author must be the\n134:        (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause) (refused :ended-lease)\n147:(defn report!\n157:   :wrong-occurrence, :not-holder, :ended-lease, :report-conflict\n161:   :suspended and :closed answers.  A refused report writes nothing.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
